    {
      "name": "workflow-schema",
      "command": "kos workflow schema",
      "source_output_sha256": "9a2420773960a101ffbe8140ea9c2f7a6a012e54d22542cf5b9a351000e60ff9",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required_fields": [
            "steps"
          ],
          "additional_fields": false,
          "steps": {
            "type": "array",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 64,
            "item": {
              "type": "object",
              "required_fields": [
                "id",
                "instruction",
                "name",
                "outcomes"
              ],
              "additional_fields": false,
              "fields": {
                "id": {
                  "type": "nonblank_utf8_string",
                  "maximum_bytes": 100
                },
                "name": {
                  "type": "nonblank_utf8_string",
                  "maximum_bytes": 200
                },
                "instruction": {
                  "type": "nonblank_utf8_string",
                  "maximum_bytes": 16384
                },
                "outcomes": {
                  "type": "nonempty_object",
                  "name_type": "nonblank_utf8_string",
                  "name_maximum_bytes": 100,
                  "total_maximum": 256,
                  "value": {
                    "exactly_one": [
                      {
                        "next_step": {
                          "type": "existing_step_id",
                          "maximum_bytes": 100
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "pause": {
                          "enum": [
                            "blocked",
                            "needs_human"
                          ]
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "complete_task": {
                          "const": true
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "rules": [
            "Step ids are unique.",
            "The first step is the initial step.",
            "Every next_step names an existing step.",
            "Every step reachable from the initial step has a path to complete_task."
          ]
        },
        "example": {
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "work",
              "name": "Work",
              "instruction": "Perform the task description and report the observed result.",
              "outcomes": {
                "completed": {
                  "complete_task": true
                },
                "question": {
                  "pause": "needs_human"
                },
                "blocked": {
                  "pause": "blocked"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "workflow-create-help",
      "command": "kos workflow create --help",
      "source_output_sha256": "e10d1ffbe81126810a66817350973b157f7d132f13d38a1fa2b9c838111414d7",
      "output": "Usage: kos workflow create [options]\n    -h, --help                       Show this help\n        --key KEY                    Required stable workflow key\n        --name NAME                  Required workflow name\n        --definition-file FILE       Required definition_json file, or - for STDIN\n\nInput definition_json is an object containing exactly steps, a non-empty array of at most 64.\nEach step contains exactly id, name, instruction, outcomes.\nid, name, instruction, and outcome names are nonblank valid UTF-8 strings.\nid and outcome names are at most 100 bytes; name is at most\n200 bytes; instruction is at most\n16384 bytes. outcomes is a non-empty object,\nwith at most 256 outcomes across the workflow. Each outcome has exactly\none transition: {\"next_step\":\"STEP_ID\"}, {\"pause\":\"needs_human\"}, {\"pause\":\"blocked\"}, or\n{\"complete_task\":true}. Step ids are unique, next_step targets exist, the first step is initial, and every\nreachable step has a path to complete_task.\nComplete valid example:\n{\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"work\",\n      \"name\": \"Work\",\n      \"instruction\": \"Perform the task description and report the observed result.\",\n      \"outcomes\": {\n        \"completed\": {\n          \"complete_task\": true\n        },\n        \"question\": {\n          \"pause\": \"needs_human\"\n        },\n        \"blocked\": {\n          \"pause\": \"blocked\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\nResponse: workflow with id, key, name, revision, definition_json, and created_at.\nExample: kos workflow create --key delivery --name Delivery --definition-file workflow.json\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "plan-put-help",
      "command": "kos plan put --help",
      "source_output_sha256": "d8f778c278c15943754a918de53d1c026c8d3c0c517da2d9aa050bb1f78ce925",
      "output": "Usage: kos plan put [options]\n    -h, --help                       Show this help\n        --project-id ID              Required numeric project ID\n        --definition-file FILE       Required plan JSON file, or - for STDIN\n\nInput object: key, title, tasks. Each task requires exactly key, title, description_markdown,\nworkflow_key, and blocker_keys. Response: task_plan with id, project_id, key, title, status, version, created_at, updated_at; tasks[] with id, key, title, description_markdown, status, current_step, claim_id, version, workflow id/key/revision, and blocker_keys.\nExample: kos plan put --project-id 7 --definition-file plan.json\n"
    },
